Hi, so I did the analysis of debt user persona - basically trying to estimate the % of user_IDs that is aware of debt and not aware of debts. And here are what I find out. Quite interesting stats imo\!

* 2M of user_IDs are currently in debt, this is around EUR 13M negative balance (the number has grown);
* Among them, 73% have logged in their App after debt and 27% haven’t;
* Among those who logged in, 23% (out of total 2M) have ordered a cash ride and 28% (out of total 2M) have tried to place an order (either in-app or cash) after

So - I think we can say that among the 2M

* Around 28% of them don’t seem to intent to pay back at all;
* It is possible that 27% don’t even know they have debt, because they haven’t logged in ever since;
* The rest of 45% have logged in and made no order ever since debt. Hard to say if they are aware of the debts. E.g. if they are just logging in to check the price, it is highly likely that they didn’t notice the negative balance at all
* If we assume it’s 50-50 in terms of aware/ not-aware in the 45% users, we are talking about potentially 45/2+27=50% of users not aware that they have negative balance in their BB accounts

To sum up - 50% not aware of negative balance, 28% not gonna pay back, and 22% are aware of negative balance.

