Hello [~accountid:61deaedbce3652006a282c65] ,

We could manage these issue / improvment point by several way and as several configuration component might be impacted, I think we need to plan a call in order to define the scope and rules.

Here are some answer (in green) to your questions :

“But my question is how WD knows that who is working with the schedule and who is not? To make this change?” {color:#36b37e}As of today, in workday, all estonian workers are supposed to work Monday to Friday. That’s why each estonian worker who is requesting a whole week (Mon to Sun) will be deduct of 5 days => Sat and Sun are not concerned. => This could be change.{color}

“In case we need to change it for all EE employees that we need to receive information about annual vacations during the weekend then how much this change will take time?” {color:#36b37e}It would depend on the scope and detailled rules needed. {color}

“The problem is that in Estonian law we have 28 calendar days vacation per year, but in WD settings we have 20 working days. By the law we still have to pay for the weekends as well (for the schedule workers) and if employee have termination then we have to pay vacation balance out as well with calendar days. So in case we don’t receive information about the annual vacations during the weekend then our vacation balances are too high.” {color:#36b37e}This can be edit but it could lead to other issue. EX : Worker accrues 28 days / year and request the whole week Mon to Sun then 7 days would be deducted. But if this worker request another week but Mon to Fri, then only 5 days would be deduct. So on both week the worker would not work for the whole week (1w : Off from Mon to Sun / 2w : Off from Mon to Fri then on weekend), but on the first week the worker would be deducted of 7 days and on the second he would be deducted of 5 days…{color}

If we need to bring a quick answer to this issue for shift worker, it should be better to create a specific work schedule calendar for them.

Could you please inform me about your avaibilities on next week, in order to plan a call ?

Regards

