Hi Darina,



Kristjan will provide broader legal perspective on this topic, but please see data protection input on the privacy-related matters below:



* What are the legal requirements when it comes to Informing the customer about the call recording;

The customers need to be informed that the recording is taking place. Before each call there should automated message informing that: (a) the call is being recorded; (b) data is processed by Bolt Operations OÜ which acts as a data controller; (c) further information on how we handle and secure personal data can be found at our website - [https://bolt.eu/en/legal/|https://bolt.eu/en/legal/|smart-link]  .

* Data retention period;

There isn’t specific retention period that is set out in applicable legislation, but general rule apply that we shouldn’t keep personal data longer than it is necessary for specific purpose. I’d usually recommend to align the retention period with the limitation period for consumer claims + additional 2 months to secure edge-cases where the claim is made by the end of the limitation period. [~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081]  - could you please a what would be applicable limitation period here?

* Data processing agreement;

Could you please specify the question here? Are we engaging any external 3rd party to handle phone support that will be processing personal data on Bolt behalf?



Kind regards,

Adriana

