So do I understand correctly that this is what the workflow should look like (at least for now)?*Markets with a dedicated (local) safety team*

* CS changes the tier to {{Safety}} and severity level to {{Minor}}
* CS Safety takes over the case and if needed, changes the severity level (if it turns out to be a significant event)

* In markets where we have FST, {{Minor}} tickets will be handled by FST. If it turns out to be a significant event, FST changes the severity to {{Severe}} and the case will be handled by IH CS Safety

*Markets without a dedicated safety team (with IST):*

* CS adds the translation of the message to the internal notes and changes the tier to {{Safety}} (should local CS select the severity or IST?)
* IST will review the case, leave instructions for the local CS and change the tier to {{Tier 1}}
* Local CS will reply to the user based on IST instructions
* Once the user replies (or the time for handling the event has passed), local CS will change the tier back to {{Safety}}

