Investigation revealed that this is concurrency issue when order gets cancelled while being processed the second time via {{createBooking}} (challenge resolve).

*Impact*: we can assume majority of users who fall into this bug get a free ride but they do accumulate debt which has to be paid later. 10-20 occurrences per week. Bug is very hard to reproduce so it would be pretty hard to abuse this vulnerability.

Agreed with the team to fix this bug right away by introducing a new booking state. This state will get assigned to booking if it is found in db during {{createBooking}} call. It has to keep booking from being cancelled when it is being processed.



Things to consider when adding new state:

* {{/getPayment}} endpoint has to be changed too, to reflect new added state;
* What should happen if new state is assigned and createBooking is called?;
* All business lines would have to know what to do with such state if it is returned (getBooking, getPayment endpoints);
* This new state cannot be final. It has to always get resolved by some process. Have to probably add it to relevant crons (ex. stuckbookingcron).

