Please note that we also consulted the Tax team recently on any implications these give-aways might have from a tax perspective - here is the advice for PT:

# If the prize of the giveaways and contests as described above would be subject to any tax, the amount and who is responsible for paying it. {color:#ff5630}*For VAT the tax treatment is the same as in the other countries - Bolt cannot deduct VAT on the purchase price of the prizes, it will remain our cost. The other tax that we need to take into account is the Stamp Duty at the rate of 45% of the value of the prize. We can pay it instead of the winners and we need to calculate it on grossed-up basis - net worth / 1 - 0,45. We need to pay the stamp duty until the 20th of the month that follows granting the prize. The regulation and practice are clear, there seems to be no way to escape the stamp duty.*{color}
# If Bolt, as the organizer of the giveaway or contest, would be obliged to withhold the winner's income tax when the value of the prize exceeds a certain amount. {color:#ff5630}*No*{color}
# Any other tax consideration we must take into account. {color:#ff5630}*No*{color}

